A||||7||William||T-top owners.....questions about Junkyard t-tops that are availible||||1||
Z||000000||William||01-28-2001||01:18 PM||||Heres the deal. Have I've gotten  price of $300 for a entire t-top roof off a junker. Does this sound reasonable? The t-top are not in great condition. The glass appears ok but one panel has been silconed in, so the seals must be bad. The interior trim is there but some of the plastic parts are cracked.<P>I see that weather seals are no longer availiable? This would seem to make t-tops worthless? What the heck do you guys do if yours go bad? Has anyone been working on a solution? Then there is the instalation nightmare. I would not want to take it to bama so I would have to go it alone. My car is nearing completion and the thought of installing old wornout and cracked pieces that leak is not pleasing. With all the frame cutting, there is also the chance that I could completely ruin a nice restored Fiero and could not undo it. That being said, I feel that T-tops would be the finest upgrade that could be done to a fiero. My biggest question is about the parts replacement problem...<P>An option to t-tops is a sunroof swap. Cheaper to do, reversible, can be done in a day, and seals are availible. The only problem with sunroofs being that they are not t-tops....<P>I need to decide before it's to late and they are gone. I'm just looking for input.||||reg||1
Z||000001||fierosound||01-28-2001||02:42 PM||||Fieroparts has an  inventory of t-top parts <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/001059.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/001059.html</A>  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||01-28-2001||06:30 PM||||300.00 isn't a bad price. Things you should look at, espically since one side has been sealed is the condition of the seals. It's quite possible that the reason for the leakage is because the trim caps, which lock the tops down, are broken. If you are going to remove it yourself, TAKE IT EASY! When removing the weather strip from around the door opening go SLOW, it will tear very easily!<BR>If you decide to buy it, send me mail and I will supply you with further tips on the removal process, or even step by step to reduce or even eliminate the possiblity of damage (I've removed 3 myself).||||reg||1
Z||000003||v8vinnie||01-28-2001||08:36 PM||||yea i too have t tops in my 87 gt, starting to wear and i guess i better start looking for new weather strips too , rainy season is coming in may in florida, but i gots to get the syspension done first.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fieroparts.com||01-28-2001||08:57 PM||||hi<P>If you need it, you better get it fast<BR>(if it is still in stock) some items that will be out of stock forever are on ebay now!<BR>I did post to this list first (on sale)<BR>not many replyed.  NOW OR NEVER!<BR>||||reg||1
